% Brief (tikz-diagram-craft). Register row ch1-16 [should].
% Reader question: what would change about the claim lifecycle if a ticket
%   queue existed, and where would it still fail?
% Claim: the designed Stigmergic Ticket-Lock covers cooperative release
%   (FIFO grant to the head of the queue) but not the lazy TTL sweep, which
%   consults no queue -- so bounded wait would hold on one exit and fail on
%   exactly the exit the kernel was built to expect.
% Evidence: whitepaper/single-writer-kernel.tex sec:op1 (Designed, not
%   shipped): claim_tickets table, the atomic release transaction (delete,
%   read lowest ticket, re-grant, remove ticket); "the sweep consults no
%   ticket queue... OP-1 stays Open until the sweep and the queue are the
%   same code path."
% Must distinguish: this is a delta on the shipped machine
%   (Figure~\ref{fig:swk-claim-lifecycle}), not a second full machine (S13:
%   no schema drawn twice); which exit is covered and which is not.
% Grammar: two small panels, same queued/held/free vocabulary, one covered
%   path and one open path. Rejected: redrawing the whole three-state
%   machine with a fourth QUEUED state added, which would repeat states
%   this figure does not change (free, expired) for one new fact.
% Five-second test: "cooperative release grants FIFO to the queue; the TTL
%   sweep skips the queue and stays open".
\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\pdfigurehue{pdcobalt}%
\begin{tikzpicture}[pd figure,x=1cm,y=1cm]
  \node[pd title,anchor=west,text width=4.4cm,align=left] at (0.00,3.15) {cooperative release: designed, covered};
  \node[pd state,minimum width=2.0cm] (q1) at (1.15,1.55) {queued (head)};
  \node[pd focus state,minimum width=2.0cm] (h1) at (4.30,1.55) {held};
  \draw[pd focus arrow] (q1) -- (h1) node[pd tag,midway,above=12pt,text width=2.0cm,align=center] {FIFO grant};

  \node[pd title,anchor=west,text width=4.4cm,align=left] at (5.75,3.15) {TTL sweep: still open (OP-1)};
  \node[pd focus state,minimum width=2.0cm] (h2) at (6.60,1.55) {held};
  \node[pd state,minimum width=2.0cm] (f2) at (9.75,1.55) {free};
  \draw[pd breach arrow] (h2) -- (f2) node[pd tag,midway,above=12pt,text width=2.5cm,align=center] {no ticket consulted};
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{The proposed ticket queue covers cooperative release, but expiry
still bypasses it. Bounded waiting remains unproved until both paths consult
the queue (\S\ref{sec:op1}). [internal]}
\label{fig:swk-ticket-lock-delta}
\end{figure}

