% Reader question: why do identical tampered token bytes pass a header-selected verifier but fail an issuer-pinned verifier?
% Claim: the paths diverge only at the source of algorithm authority: attacker-controlled header versus issuer policy.
% Evidence: alg=none tampered payload in Phase 1 and the ProVerif v1 secrecy query [verified, v1_refined.pv].
% Must distinguish: identical wire bytes, algorithm source, signature-check reachability, and accept/reject outcome.
% Grammar: aligned paired security trace on shared rows; rejected stacked sequence ladders because their height hid the one changed control point.
% Five-second test: one shared input fans into equal-width traces; header authority ends in accept, issuer authority ends in signature failure and reject.
\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\pdfigurehue{pdcobalt}%
\begin{tikzpicture}[pd figure,x=1cm,y=1cm]
  \def\xL{2.48}
  \def\xR{8.18}

