% Brief (grammar: paired before/after panels, same chain geometry, different
%   check edges; new addition -- register item "v6-vs-v7 escalation chains,"
%   the chapter's only figure-free treatment of a fully evidenced result.
%   Facts: \S "Multi-hop scope" and the v6/v7 pdexample pair, chain
%   A:write -> B:read -> C:write, files harbor_card_v6_multihop_attack.pv /
%   harbor_card_v7_multihop_fixed.pv [internal].
% Reader question: why does checking the final capability against the root
%   miss a re-escalating middle hop that checking each hop against its
%   parent catches?
% Claim: A:write -> B:read -> C:write is accepted when the verifier compares
%   only final-vs-root (write subset write, trivially true) and rejected the
%   moment the verifier compares final-vs-immediate-parent (write is not a
%   subset of read).
% Evidence: harbor_card_v6_multihop_attack.pv (escalation reachable);
%   harbor_card_v7_multihop_fixed.pv (same chain, rejected) [internal].
% Must distinguish: the SHAPE of the check (which edge the verifier actually
%   compares), not the chain itself, which is identical in both panels --
%   only the comparison target changes.
% Grammar chosen: before/after on identical chain geometry (tpl-before-after).
%   Rejected: a state machine per verifier -- the chain has only three nodes
%   and one comparison choice; a machine would add apparatus the two-panel
%   comparison does not need.
% Five-second test: "same three-node chain in both panels; v6 checks C
%   straight against A and accepts; v7 checks B against A and C against B,
%   and the second check fails."
