% Brief (tikz-diagram-craft), register row ch4-27.
% Reader question: when a blinded, ground-truth-known defect is replayed to
%   the operator, does the response tighten or loosen the daemons trust in
%   them?
% Claim: the Inception Canary replays a known, already-fixed defect into a
%   sandboxed replay at a disclosed rate, surfaces it in the attention
%   queue like live traffic, and adjudicates the operators response as
%   either a rubber-stamp failure (halt, tighten lease) or a vigilant
%   detection (log defeated, widen grant) -- never a silent third option.
% Evidence: Protocol The Inception Canary protocol, prot:canary,
%   whitepaper/legible-swarm.tex sec 4.5.4 (this pass).
% Must distinguish: the two adjudication outcomes and their opposite
%   effects on the operators autonomous policy lease; that the probe is a
%   replay with known ground truth, never a live pull request.
% Grammar chosen: protocol/decision flow, three ordered steps into a single
%   two-way adjudication gate, each outcome badged with its trust effect.
% Grammar rejected: a two-state trust-score time series would need a
%   measurement this hypothesis-stage mechanism does not have yet; the
%   protocol itself, not its (unmeasured) effect over time, is what the
%   chapter actually specifies.
% Five-second test: does approving without expanding the diff tighten or
